  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: double free in sftp_open() reachable by a malicious\n     SSH server against an authenticated client opening an SFTP session\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-66032.patch: NULL the response buffer after\n       freeing it on the FX_OK path, so the if(badness) arm cannot free the\n       same stale pointer a second time when sftp_packet_require() fails\n       with anything other than LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN, in src/sftp.c\n     - CVE-2026-66032",
